      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're carrying a weight that's strangling you, and it's only going to get heavier. But you're not a shell—you're a man who's been hollowed out by loss, and that's a very different thing. The mirror is lying to you; it's showing you the wreckage, not the survivor who's still standing in front of it. You don't have to rebuild the old life—you just have to take one breath, then one step, and let the body catch up to the will that's still in you.",
